{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1562132-hunger-system-homebrew-feedback-welcome","id":1562132,"title":"Hunger System Homebrew - Feedback Welcome","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-24T13:45:28-07:00","id":1562132,"title":"Hunger System Homebrew - Feedback Welcome","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I\u2019ve been playing Requiem with Hunger dice rules for quite a while now.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">The basic idea was very similar to v5, with some minor tweaks :</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">If you have a 1 on a hunger die and no successes, you\u2019d have a bestial failure, or if you rolled a 10 on a hunger dice that exploded into another success, you\u2019d get a messy success.</span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I\u2019ve enjoyed it for a few reasons:</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">It gives a visual representation of hunger.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">It makes the beast\u2019s urges feel a lot more present.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Disciplines and blood surge now involve a risk rather the calculated decisions that the vitae pools grant. </span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">The system isn\u2019t without \u2018\u2019jank\u2019\u2019, however.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Indeed, I think the frequent penalty that requiem imposes on tests makes it a bit awkward when hunger is high. Indeed, a character with a decent skill pool has between 4 and 6 dice. As soon as I applied a penalty, it became a bit awkward, as most dice ended up being hunger dice, so any exceptional success carried the taint of the beast. It didn't feel good.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I also feel like bestial failures were a bit <i>too </i>frequent to my taste.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I decided to refine the system into a single dice. I called the \u2018\u2019Bestial dice\u2019\u2019, which I\u2019ll have to test in my next session.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">My idea was to reduce the number of hunger dice to a single die handling the bestial urge, while still keeping the hunger and rouse check system.</span> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:26px\">Bestial Die</span></b><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">When a vampire makes a test, treat one die from their pool as their bestial dice; it functions as a regular dice, except for the extra effects detailed below. If their pool is only one dice, roll the bestial dice apart from the last dice. Ignore any success it might give.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">When a character rolls a 1 on their bestial dice. Roll a d10. If they roll a number that\u2019s <i>lower </i>than twice their current hunger, their test becomes bestial.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Bestial Result :</b> The beast has wants that rarely align with a vampire\u2019s goal and the hungrier they feel, the louder it screams from the back of their mind. A bestial result means that the character has let their beast\u2019s influence take its hold.<br /> <br /> This is usually represented in one of the following ways :</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">They might gain any of the bestial triad conditions (Bestial, Competitive or Wanton) for the rest of the scene. Based on what they were trying to achieve. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">They might gain any other conditions, such as obsessed, swooning, etc. They also last for a scene.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">They make a flat rouse check if their hunger increases. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">They might need to make a frenzy test if they are already hungry, or in a stressful scene.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Or their success might be influenced by the beast : like successfully picklocking a door by ripping the handle off, persuading someone by relying on intimidation instead of careful arguments, etc. In the case of an empathy test, the beast might focus on ways to exploit the target instead of their emotional state.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">A failure might provoke a frenzy. </span></li> </ul></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">A player is also free to come up with ideas.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Satisfying the Beast</b><br /> If the character acts in accordance with the beast\u2019s want, they can regain a point of willpower, once per scene.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">For example, if the beast wants to frenzy, a character regains a point of willpower by opting to give in. If the beasts inflicts the Competitive condition, the character regains willpower if they assert their dominance, etc.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">If the beasts need are unclear, such as turning a success messy. The storyteller can award willpower for good roleplay.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Ghouls and Bestial Dice</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Ghouls also rolls a bestial dice. On a roll of 1, instead of rolling against their hunger, if their d10 result is lower than their resolve + composure, they suffer a complication. Usually manifesting in conditions or behaviour that represents their vitae addicted nature.</span></div> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-size:26px\">Hunger</span></b><br /> </div> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Hunger replaces vitae reserve. It has a score from 0 to 5. Feeding cannot reduce hunger below 1 unless it\u2019s from vitae, or from killing a human. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">At hunger 4, a kindred is considered hungry (-2) and at hunger 5 they are considered starving (-4).</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Unless mentioned otherwise, if hunger would increase past 5, the kindred suffers a point of lethal damage instead.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Rouse Check</b> <br /> A rouse check is a single d10 roll. On a roll of 5 or lower, the kindred\u2019s hunger increases by 1. A vampire can\u2019t voluntarily trigger a rouse check at hunger 5.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Vitae Cost to Rouse Check conversion</b></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #e97132\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">Vitae Cost</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #e97132\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">Rouse Check</span></b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #fae2d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">1</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #fae2d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><span style=\"color:black\">1</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>2</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Roll an extra die, keep the worst.</span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #fae2d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">3+</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #fae2d5\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><span style=\"color:black\">Half vitae cost, rounded up</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Feeding </b><br /> Satiating one point of hunger requires inflicting 1 point of lethal damage per vitae potency, with a feeding move, which inflicts 1 lethal per turn. <br /> <br /> <b>Waking up</b><br /> To wake up, a vampire needs to make a rouse check. If they fail that check while at hunger 5, they fall into torpor.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Stealing &amp; Sharing Vitae</b> <br /> When feeding on another kindred, the vampire that\u2019s feeding need to spend 1 turn feeding per their vitae potency score to reduce their hunger by 1. Each hunger reduced that way count as 1 vitae for the purpose of blood addiction &amp; Blood Bound. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">The vampire that\u2019s being drained increase their hunger by 1 after a number of turns equal to their vitae potency, if it\u2019s lower than their vitae potency, they simply need to make a rouse check. If a vampire is already at hunger 5, feeding on them inflicts them with 1 lethal per turn spent feeding, which does not satiate hunger. Which can lead to torpor, or diablerie if the vampire keeps on sucking. (See diablerie VTR: 101) </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Ghouls </b> <br /> Can store a number of rouses check worth of vitae equal to half their stamina, rounded up. Each month they need to make a rouse check to maintain their ghoul status. They cannot make a rouse check if they have no more vitae stored.</span> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:26px\">Blood Potency</span></b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2\" align=\"center\" style=\"width: 737px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #680000\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">Blood</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">Potency</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #680000\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">Blood </span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">Surge</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #680000\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">Damage Mended</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">(B/L)</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #680000\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\"> Discipline</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">Reduction</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #680000\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">Maximum rouse check per Turn</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #680000\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">Vitae Potency</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #680000\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">Sunlight Damage</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">Frequency</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #680000\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:white\">Feeding Restriction</span></b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffb3b3\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b><span style=\"color:black\">0*</span></b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffb3b3\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><span style=\"color:black\">2 </span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffb3b3\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><span style=\"color:black\">2/1</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffb3b3\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><span style=\"color:black\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffb3b3\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><span style=\"color:black\">1</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffb3b3\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><span style=\"color:black\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffb3b3\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><span style=\"color:black\">-</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\" style=\"background-color: #ffb3b3\"><span style=\"font-size:9px\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><span style=\"color:black\">None</span></span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4Accent2_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>1</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_MsoTable15Grid4